        "ImageDescription": {
          "value": "Two stacks (unwrapped rolls) of American <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Half_dollar_(United_States_coin)\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:Half dollar (United States coin)\">half dollars</a>, demonstrating the effects of the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coinage_Act_of_1965\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:Coinage Act of 1965\">Coinage Act of 1965</a> in action \u2013 the stack of clad post-1971 half dollars can instantly be recognized by the reddish-brown copper cores visible from the edges of each coin, while the silver <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Walking_Liberty_half_dollar\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:Walking Liberty half dollar\">Walking Liberty half dollars</a> have bright white edges and faces.",
